`CloudNimble.Text.Xml` is the main namespace of XmlEssentials. It holds the four ways to work with XML, all of them over UTF-8 and all of them shaped like their counterparts in `System.Text.Json`:

| To do this | Use | Like |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Convert between your types and XML | [`XmlSerializer`](/api-reference/CloudNimble/Text/Xml/XmlSerializer) | `JsonSerializer` |
| Parse a document and query it | [`XmlDocument`](/api-reference/CloudNimble/Text/Xml/XmlDocument) and [`XmlElement`](/api-reference/CloudNimble/Text/Xml/XmlElement) | `JsonDocument` and `JsonElement` |
| Read XML one token at a time | [`Utf8XmlReader`](/api-reference/CloudNimble/Text/Xml/Utf8XmlReader) | `Utf8JsonReader` |
| Write XML one call at a time | [`Utf8XmlWriter`](/api-reference/CloudNimble/Text/Xml/Utf8XmlWriter) | `Utf8JsonWriter` |

The tree that you can change, `XmlNode`, is in `CloudNimble.Text.Xml.Nodes`. Attributes, converters, and source generation support are in `CloudNimble.Text.Xml.Serialization`. Nothing in the library depends on `System.Xml`.
